					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-231140#post-3894003</guid>
				<title>Page Image</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-231140/scp-777-j#post-3894003</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 01 Aug 2018 11:40:56 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>DrArmstrong</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>420092</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Hey everybody,</p> <p>When I made this SCP a little over eight years ago I hopped on to Google Image and searched “Sephiroth fanart” (who better to represent an edgy, mary-sue, “original character”?) and selected the page image with little thought other than “That’ll work!”. Since then the wiki has grown a lot and with it the enforcement of Creative Commons has necessarily grown more important, which brings me to the rub&#8230;</p> <p>The page image is not licensed under Creative Commons and I do not have permission to use it. To be clear, I have not been approached by the artist (or anyone) regarding the use of the drawing, and my attempts to contact the artist have lead me to a deadend in the form of a seven-years-inactive DeviantArt page.</p> <p>Therefore, I am stating my intent to replace the page image with something new. It could be art of Sephiroth, actual art of Darkblade, or even a cosplay photo, just so long as I have permission to use it. Obviously this isn’t high on the community’s priority list, but I still feel it’s important.</p> <p>Anyone who has an idea of a usable image or would like to create one can contact me here, or on my tumblr (bionicle.tumblr.com) or twitter (@PerogiXW).</p> <p>Cheers!</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
